@PlayerId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Career of a player, newest season first (take the id from GET /players; defaults: offset 0, limit 25)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters
Accept: application/json

### Oldest season first
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?sort=season,memberFrom
Accept: application/json

### Page through the career
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?offset=0&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### Offset beyond the end: 200 with empty items, not an error
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?offset=10000
Accept: application/json

### Error: the player does not exist (404)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/rosters
Accept: application/json

### Error: the player id is not a GUID (404, the route does not match)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/not-a-guid/rosters
Accept: application/json

### Error: unknown sort field (400, errors.sort)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?sort=name
Accept: application/json

### Error: limit above the maximum of 100 (400, errors.limit)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?limit=1000
Accept: application/json

### Error: negative offset (400, errors.offset)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/players/{{PlayerId}}/rosters?offset=-1
Accept: application/json
